<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-1607] Implement deadlock-free optimistic serializable mode</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-1607</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;There is an idea of optimistic serializable mode which will provide better scalability on relatively large transactions and large topologies when no heavy contention is experienced.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;When transactional read is performed, we need to store the version of read entry.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;When transaction prepare is performed, we can send prepare requests simultaneously on all nodes. There is no need to preserve the order of locks and create a queue of tx mappings for this mode.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;When we add local MVCC candidates on a primary node, two checks are performed: that the current entry version matches the one transaction read (if read was performed), and that currently there are no other local MVCC candidates. If any of these checks fails, prepare step fails and transaction is failed with optimistic conflict exception.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
</description>
                <environment></environment>
